<title>GERMANY: German builders continue protests, wage talks due.</title>
<headline>German builders continue protests, wage talks due.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Several thousand German construction workers on Thursday continued protests in Berlin over the mass unemployment in the sector and so-called &quot;wage-dumping&quot; by foreign firms in the sector.</p>
<p>The protests came as employers and trade union officials were due to meet in Frankfurt for the second round of wage talks after an earlier round in February was adjourned without agreement.</p>
<p>The IG Bau trade union is seeking new clauses compensating workers for pay lost as a result of poor weather and a reinstatement of an earlier &quot;13th month&quot; bonus that employers have cancelled from existing contracts.</p>
<p>IG Bau has not as yet expressed a precise wage increase demand in the sector but has said its aim is that wages should not fall &quot;in real terms&quot;.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
